string.text:
Among the many pages of obscure terminology, diagrams, and barely legible illustrations, a typewritten sheet titled “Conclusion on the bio-breeding project” stands out. 

“Following an audit of the project conducted by the Department of Bio-breeding and Eugenics at the “ZX-08” complex, the commission concluded that: 

1) the project is still in the early stages of implementation; 

2) it is paramount that a method that combines the development of the mental abilities of the test subjects and the effective masking of the outer cortex radiation is created; 

3) it is recommended that the neuroengineering department is brought up to speed on the issue of the psychotronic overload for consultation purposes; 

4) the accumulation of test subjects within the “ZX-08” complex poses significant risks to the project and its personnel; 

5) it is recommended that a meeting be held to address the implementation of regular disposal of the biomaterial. 

June 6, 1995”
